# Caddyfile — reverse proxy + automatic HTTPS for Shopfloor ERP (prod only).
#
# Used by the `caddy` service in docker-compose.prod.yml. Caddy v2 gets TLS
# "for free": when a Caddyfile's site address is a real domain name (not an
# IP or `localhost`), Caddy automatically requests and renews a Let's
# Encrypt certificate for it via the ACME HTTP-01 challenge on port 80, then
# serves HTTPS on 443 — no manual certbot, no cert files to manage, no TLS
# config to write. It just needs the domain's DNS A record already pointed
# at this droplet's IP (see the README's Deployment runbook, step 2) so
# Let's Encrypt's validation request can reach this container.
#
# {$DOMAIN} is a Caddyfile env-var substitution: it reads the DOMAIN
# variable that docker-compose.prod.yml passes into the caddy service's
# environment (itself sourced from the droplet's .env).

{$DOMAIN}
reverse_proxy app:8000

# --- No-domain fallback (documented in requirements/11-deployment.md) ------
# If you don't have a domain to point at the droplet yet, comment out the
# two lines above and uncomment the block below instead: it serves plain
# HTTP on port 80 at the droplet's bare IP, with no certificate involved.
# Acceptable for a short-lived demo; prefer the domain above when you can —
# automatic HTTPS on a demo built in a few hours is a strong signal in
# itself.
#
# http:// {
#     reverse_proxy app:8000
# }
